public sealed class WindowsSecurityPostureProvider(IPowerShellRunner ps,IAdministratorService admin):ISecurityPostureProvider{private const string Script="""$c=@();function Add($name,$state,$supported,$managed,$policy,$detail,$source,$requirements){$script:c+=[pscustomobject]@{control=$name;state=$state;supported=$supported;managed=$managed;policy=$policy;detail=$detail;source=$source;requirements=$requirements}};try{$m=Get-MpComputerStatus -ErrorAction Stop;Add 'DefenderAntivirus' $(if($m.AntivirusEnabled -and $m.RealTimeProtectionEnabled){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $false '' 'Microsoft Defender Antivirus and real-time protection state.' 'Get-MpComputerStatus' @()}catch{Add 'DefenderAntivirus' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Defender provider unavailable; another antivirus or edition policy may apply.' 'Get-MpComputerStatus' @()};try{$f=Get-NetFirewallProfile -ErrorAction Stop;Add 'Firewall' $(if(@($f|Where-Object Enabled).Count-eq@($f).Count){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true ($f.PolicyStoreSourceType-contains'GroupPolicy') 'Windows Firewall policy store' 'Domain, Private, and Public profile state.' 'Get-NetFirewallProfile' @()}catch{Add 'Firewall' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Firewall provider unavailable.' 'Get-NetFirewallProfile' @()};try{$sb=Confirm-SecureBootUEFI -ErrorAction Stop;Add 'SecureBoot' $(if($sb){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $false '' 'UEFI Secure Boot state.' 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI' @('UEFI firmware')}catch{Add 'SecureBoot' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Secure Boot is unavailable or permission was denied.' 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI' @('UEFI firmware')};try{$t=Get-Tpm -ErrorAction Stop;Add 'Tpm' $(if($t.TpmReady){'Enabled'}elseif($t.TpmPresent){'Disabled'}else{'NotApplicable'}) ([bool]$t.TpmPresent) $false '' 'TPM presence and readiness.' 'Get-Tpm' @('Compatible TPM')}catch{Add 'Tpm' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'TPM provider unavailable.' 'Get-Tpm' @('Compatible TPM')};try{$b=Get-BitLockerVolume -ErrorAction Stop|Where-Object VolumeType-eq'OperatingSystem'|Select-Object -First 1;Add 'DeviceEncryption' $(if($b.ProtectionStatus-eq'On'){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $false '' 'Operating-system volume protection.' 'Get-BitLockerVolume' @('Supported Windows edition','TPM or approved key protector')}catch{Add 'DeviceEncryption' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Encryption status unavailable for this edition or permission level.' 'Get-BitLockerVolume' @('Supported Windows edition')};$dg=Get-CimInstance Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\Microsoft\Windows\DeviceGuard -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue;if($dg){Add 'CoreIsolation' $(if($dg.SecurityServicesRunning-contains2){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $false '' 'Memory integrity / HVCI state.' 'Win32_DeviceGuard' @('Virtualization support');Add 'CredentialGuard' $(if($dg.SecurityServicesRunning-contains1){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $false '' 'Credential Guard runtime state.' 'Win32_DeviceGuard' @('Supported Windows edition','Virtualization support')}else{Add 'CoreIsolation' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Device Guard provider unavailable.' 'Win32_DeviceGuard' @('Virtualization support');Add 'CredentialGuard' 'Unavailable' $false $false '' 'Device Guard provider unavailable.' 'Win32_DeviceGuard' @('Supported Windows edition')};$u=Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue;Add 'Uac' $(if($null-eq$u.EnableLUA){'Unknown'}elseif($u.EnableLUA){'Enabled'}else{'Disabled'}) $true $true 'HKLM policy' 'User Account Control policy state.' 'Registry:Policies:System' @();$s=Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue;Add 'SmartScreen' $(if($null-eq$s.SmartScreenEnabled){'Unknown'}elseif($s.SmartScreenEnabled-eq'Off'){'Disabled'}else{'Enabled'}) $true $false '' 'SmartScreen shell policy state.' 'Registry:Explorer' @();$r=(Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\WindowsUpdate\Auto Update' -Name RebootRequired -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue);Add 'WindowsUpdates' 'Unknown' $true $false '' 'Use Update Health for detailed freshness and servicing evidence.' 'Windows Update local state' @();[pscustomobject]@{edition=(Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).Caption;controls=$c}|ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6 -Compress""";public async Task<SecurityPostureSnapshot> CollectAsync(CancellationToken t){var r=await ps.RunAsync(Script,new Dictionary<string,object?>(),t);if(!r.Succeeded)throw new SecurityPostureException("WAID-SECURITY-COLLECT","Windows security posture could not be collected.",string.Join("; ",r.Errors));var p=JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Payload>(string.Join(Environment.NewLine,r.Output),new JsonSerializerOptions{PropertyNameCaseInsensitive=true})??throw new SecurityPostureException("WAID-SECURITY-DATA","Windows returned empty security posture data.","No payload.");var controls=(p.Controls??[]).Where(x=>Enum.TryParse<SecurityControl>(x.Control,true,out _)).Select(x=>new SecurityControlStatus(Enum.Parse<SecurityControl>(x.Control!,true),Enum.TryParse<SecurityState>(x.State,true,out var s)?s:SecurityState.Unknown,x.Supported,x.Managed,Clean(x.Policy),Clean(x.Detail),Clean(x.Source),(x.Requirements??[]).Select(Clean).ToArray())).ToArray();return new(DateTimeOffset.UtcNow,controls,admin.IsAdministrator(),Clean(p.Edition),admin.IsAdministrator()?[]:["Standard-user collection can make encryption, Secure Boot, TPM, and policy details unavailable; unavailable is not disabled."]);}private static string Clean(string? x)=>((x??"").Replace(Environment.UserName,"[user]",StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)).Trim();private sealed record Payload(string? Edition,ControlDto[]? Controls);private sealed record ControlDto(string? Control,string? State,bool Supported,bool Managed,string? Policy,string? Detail,string? Source,string[]? Requirements);}
public sealed class SecurityPostureAnalyzer(ISecurityPostureProvider provider,ISecurityPostureRepository repo,ILogger<SecurityPostureAnalyzer> log):ISecurityPostureAnalyzer{public async Task<SecurityPostureReport> AnalyzeAsync(CancellationToken t){var s=await provider.CollectAsync(t);var findings=Evaluate(s);var previous=await repo.GetLatestAsync(t);var report=new SecurityPostureReport(Guid.NewGuid(),s.CollectedAtUtc,s.Controls,findings,previous?.AcknowledgedExceptions??[],s.Limitations);await repo.SaveAsync(s,report,t);log.LogInformation("Security posture {ReportId} stored {ControlCount} controls and {FindingCount} findings",report.Id,report.Controls.Count,report.Findings.Count);return report;}public static IReadOnlyList<SecurityFinding> Evaluate(SecurityPostureSnapshot s)=>s.Controls.Where(x=>x.State==SecurityState.Disabled).Select(x=>new SecurityFinding(x.Control,$"{Display(x.Control)} is off",$"Windows reports {Display(x.Control)} as disabled. WAID does not replace Windows Security and will never weaken this control.",x.Control is SecurityControl.DefenderAntivirus or SecurityControl.Firewall?"Critical":"Warning",.95,[new("state","Disabled",x.SourceReference,s.CollectedAtUtc)],x.IsPolicyManaged,x.IsPolicyManaged?"This setting is policy-managed. Contact the administrator; WAID will not bypass the lock.":$"Open the supported Windows Security or Settings page for {Display(x.Control)} after confirming prerequisites.",x.Prerequisites)).ToArray();private static string Display(SecurityControl c)=>c switch{SecurityControl.Uac=>"User Account Control",SecurityControl.Tpm=>"TPM",_=>c.ToString()};}
